# What scripts/build-kosmickrisp.sh builds. Mesa main from 30.10.2026: KosmicKrisp has advertised
# geometryShader since 14f59d06 (29.10.), which DXVK's Direct3D 9 needs next to shaderCullDistance.
# The loader and its headers are the Khronos release that matches Mesa's Vulkan headers.
MESA_URL=https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa.git
MESA_COMMIT=44989e5a489c0ddbc79d2019f2c236699251c69e
VULKAN_LOADER_URL=https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Loader.git
VULKAN_LOADER_COMMIT=aa6dee8385afe4b2cc0152d086af2184743e16fd
VULKAN_HEADERS_URL=https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Headers.git
VULKAN_HEADERS_COMMIT=9fbc2a782ee3f8a4db64e7d991e23da75e893f44
# patches/ carries two Mesa changes by Nilton Perim Neto (Signed-off-by, from dappermint/winecx-gptk's
# KosmicKrisp lane, not in Mesa yet): 0001 fillModeNonSolid through Metal's triangle fill mode (DXVK
# 2 and later won't create a device without it), 0002 the memory budget under Rosetta (a quarter of
# the real value before: x86_64 sees 4 KiB pages, the kernel counts 16 KiB ones).
